# Insoora marketing site — environment
#
# Copy to `.env.local` for development. On Vercel, set these under
# Project → Settings → Environment Variables, for BOTH Production and
# Preview. Both are NEXT_PUBLIC_ and therefore inlined at BUILD time:
# changing either needs a redeploy, not a restart.

# ── Where the product lives ──────────────────────────────────────────────
# THE ONE VALUE THAT REALLY HAS TO BE SET. Every "Sign in" and "Get Started"
# control points into this origin, and /api/enquiries relays the contact form
# to it server-side.
#
# Unset in production, the build does NOT fail — it logs a warning and falls
# back to the value below, which is this project's intended host as recorded
# here. It never falls back to localhost: when it did, the deployed site
# served `http://localhost:3000/agent/register` on every primary button.
#
# Confirm the host below actually resolves and serves the product. At the time
# of writing it does not, because the domain is not connected yet — so until
# it is, set this to wherever the product is really reachable, or accept that
# the conversion path leads somewhere that is not answering yet. Check the
# deploy log for the warning.
NEXT_PUBLIC_APP_URL=https://app.insoora.com

# ── This site's own public origin ────────────────────────────────────────
# OPTIONAL, AND THE INDEXING SWITCH.
#
# Canonical URLs, Open Graph URLs, sitemap.xml and robots.txt are built from
# it. Leave it UNSET until the real domain is actually connected and serving:
#
#   unset  → canonicals fall back to the deployment's own Vercel production
#            host (never localhost; off Vercel, to the domain below), and
#            every page is noindex, robots.txt disallows everything and the
#            sitemap is empty. That stops the *.vercel.app copy being indexed
#            and then having to be de-indexed once the real domain goes live.
#   set    → that domain becomes the canonical origin and the whole site
#            becomes indexable. Only set it when the domain resolves.
#
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=https://www.insoora.com

# ── Legal review callouts ────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The Privacy Policy and Terms pages are drafts, and the sections still
# needing a real fact or a legal decision render as visible "Needs review"
# callouts. Set this to `off` ONLY once that review is actually done — it is
# a deliberate act by whoever completed it, not a build-time tidy-up.
# LEGAL_REVIEW_FLAGS=off
